    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test class \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 passing).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**1. `AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 in addition to the existing human-readable audit line (unchanged), it now emits an immutable structured JSON event on the same `AUDIT` logger:\n\n```json\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n- `seq` comes from a static `AtomicLong` (`incrementAndGet`), so it's monotonically increasing across every create in the process.\n- The JSON is built with Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson.databind`, already a main-scope dependency) as an `ObjectNode`, serialized once \u2014 a self-contained, immutable record.\n\n**2. `OwnerPrimaryIdentifier.java`** (new) \u2014 a single source of truth for the owner's *primary identifier*. The event sources its identifier through `OwnerPrimaryIdentifier.of(owner)` rather than reading `customerCode` inline.\n\nThat abstraction is the point of the forward-compat requirement: today `of(owner)` returns the `customerCode`, so the event carries the customerCode (which the test asserts against the owner's `customerCode` JSON field). When the customerCode is later unified into the `memberId`, only that one method changes to return the `memberId`, and the audit event automatically carries the new identifier without touching `AuditOwnerCreated` or any other consumer.\n\nThe `audit` step already runs after `recordIdempotency` and before `respond` in `owners.POST.yml`, so no wiring changes were needed.",
